# interplay_iosfcwalk_19: Seeded walks over the IOSurface host device and its consumers (pgtest/iosfcwalk_util.py): each seed is one scenario, interplay_iosfcwalk_<seed>, whose program the walker builds from the seed alone.  The IOSurface host device QEMU's apple-gfx-mmio creates beside the RvgDevice (docs/testing.md 6.23) is driven at random through its ring and registers: batches of map, unmap and test commands with bad ids, ids whose descriptor page the table does not name, an invalid descriptor and unknown commands; the ring moved to rings of other sizes with the counters kept, commands written into the old ring and rung after the move, the read counter rewound (commands run again) or moved past commands never rung, a doorbell while no ring is mapped; the descriptor table rewritten (every surface dropped) and the descriptor format switched with a doorbell before the new table. Interleaved with its consumers: a GPU task per surface filling and copying into it through a mapper buffer (type 15), deleted (37) and made again; opcode 8 presents of the surfaces and opcode 7 presents of task 0's backings on one or two heads; work held on a gate FIFO or rung while paused while the guest unmaps, remaps, tests, rewrites or tears down the surfaces it names (a fill whose buffer is not made faults its child when its id has no surface; a present of such an id is refused); and the device's lifecycle: pause with the IOSurface device and the guest busy, the suspend onto a fresh device with work held across it, and reset with the guest's set-up again.  The model predicts every ring entry's status, the descriptors' mapped bits, the registers, every surface's bytes (against a mirror page), every frame the heads encode, the callbacks and IOSurface interrupts at every checkpoint, and which work runs, faults or is refused; every wait succeeds but those labelled [held] (work shown not to run within 300 ms) and [dies]. python3 -m pgtest.iosfcwalk_util reads the expected files back against it. Map and isolate only: the IOSurface host device needs a memory map (apple-gfx-mmio.c:134-162). Some programs end in a death with work held on the gate: the ring's size written unaligned (the memory map asserts), a present of a 16400-pixel-wide surface (Metal aborts making its texture), a second pause.  This program: ports=2; descriptors v1; ids 5,47,100; ring 2048; gate p 0.5; lifecycle weight 1.5. Steps: 37 6, fault 16, fill 92, format switched 3, gate opened 15, pause 27, present 30, refused present 5, registers 2, reset 6, rewrite 28, ring 115, ring moved 20, ring moved before the doorbell 8, ring rewound 8, ring skipped 5, rung unmapped 6, setups diverged 6, suspend 15, teardown 13.
